  "title": "Sticky Cantor sets",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Let $C$ be a Cantor set embedded in $\\mathbb{R}^n$. Is there a self-homeomorphism $f$ of $\\mathbb{R}^n$ for every $\\epsilon$ greater than $0$ so that $f$ moves every point by less than $\\epsilon$ and $f(C)$ does not intersect $C$? Such an embedded Cantor set for which no such $f$ exists (for some $\\epsilon$ ) is called \"sticky\". For what dimensions $n$ do sticky Cantor sets exist?",
